From 26937d7630709c1897c2ceb55d893644b37630ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:22:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 136/171] ruletext: domains of a text list built in place by
 common/domainset

The names of a list written as text go to the collector of
common/domainset where they are in the content: a line is no longer a
string, a name in lower case is not copied, repeats are dropped as the
trie is built instead of by a map. The rule carries the matcher
(DomainMatcher). Only items that may be addresses (a colon, or digits,
dots and a slash only) are tried as such. Items not of ASCII take the
former way, strings.ToLower included.

ReadAddresses reads a list without building its domains, for a caller
that wants only the addresses and whether sing-box takes the list.
